WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.092 --> 00:00:07.182
Fixer Nation Education has a few different sign in pages, and this video helps you pick the right one.

2
00:00:07.685 --> 00:00:17.615
Look at the footer at the bottom of any page. The Access column lists Student Login, Teacher Login, Parent Portal, School Admin, and District Admin.

3
00:00:18.115 --> 00:00:28.365
The Log In menu at the top of the page has entries for teachers, students, parents, and school administrators. District administrators sign in from the footer link.

4
00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:35.687
Teachers sign in with an email address and a password. After you sign in, you land on your classrooms.

5
00:00:36.188 --> 00:00:50.068
School license administrators use the School Admin page. It checks that your account really is set up as an administrator. If it isn't, you'll see a message that tells you to contact us. Here, a teacher's account tries it.

6
00:00:50.571 --> 00:00:55.611
District administrators use the District Admin page, which works the same way.

7
00:00:56.113 --> 00:01:10.383
Students don't use an email at all. They sign in with a username and a P-I-N. A student who is new joins a class with a code from their teacher, and a student who already has an account selects Sign In with Username and P-I-N.

8
00:01:10.884 --> 00:01:16.424
Parents use the Parent Login page, with the email address their child's teacher invited.

9
00:01:16.925 --> 00:01:28.145
One email address can hold more than one role. If you're a teacher and also a school administrator, you use the same email and password. The page you choose decides where you land.
